---
// Contact (DESIGN_BRIEF.md 5.7). "This is a qualification form, not a booking
// link. Its job is to filter." Three parts, in the brief's order: the paragraph
// explaining what the consultation is, the form, then the FAQ.
//
// The intro paragraph is the most rule-bound copy on the site. 5.7: say it is a
// paid in-home visit; do NOT say the fee credits toward the project (rule 2 —
// it does not); do not apologise for the fee; do not state the amount until Amy
// confirms one (open in ASK-AMY.md). The paragraph below does all four by
// describing what the visit buys and stopping there.
//
// **Two deliberate omissions, both interpretations rather than oversights:**
// - No lead image. Every other text-led page opens with one, but 5.7 does not
//   ask for one and the site has three usable photographs total, each already
//   doing three or four jobs. A fifth reuse would add nothing here. Revisit once
//   Kelsee's shoot lands (IMAGE-MANIFEST.md).
// - No phone number or email on the page. The footer already carries contact
//   details (5.1). Putting them beside the form would give a reader a way around
//   the filter the brief says this page exists to be.

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ConsultationForm from '../components/ConsultationForm.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Schedule a Consultation | Amy K Clark Design"
  description="Request an in-home consultation for custom drapery, blinds and shades, upholstery, or soft furnishings in Cincinnati and Northern Kentucky."
  ogImage="/images/og/og-default.jpg"
  transparentNav={false}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Contact', href: '/contact' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section wrap text-page__intro">
    <p class="type-label text-page__eyebrow">Contact</p>
    <h1 class="type-display text-page__heading">Schedule a Consultation</h1>
    <p class="text-page__lead">
      Every project starts with a paid in-home visit. Amy comes to the room, measures the openings
      herself, sees the light at the hour that matters, and puts fabric against your walls and your
      furniture. You come out of it knowing what the room needs and what she would do about it.
    </p>
    <p class="contact__lead-continued">
      The form below is how she works out whether she is the right person for your project before
      either of you spends a morning finding out. The more you can tell her about the room, the more
      useful the visit will be.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap contact__form-section" aria-labelledby="form-heading">
    <h2 id="form-heading" class="type-display contact__form-heading">Tell me about your room</h2>
    <ConsultationForm />
  </section>

  <Faq />
</Base>

<style>
  .contact__lead-continued {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  /* The form section follows the intro immediately, so it drops the leading
     section pad rather than stacking 160px on top of 160px. */
  .contact__form-section {
    padding-block-start: 0;
  }

  .contact__form-heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2.25rem);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
